# 148 - Treasure Chest Shared Loot System

## Status
- Created: 2026-04-04
- Phase: 2
- Priority: Medium

## Current Behavior
- Treasure chests spawn with loot
- Single player opens chest, takes what they want
- Remaining loot disappears when chest closes/despawns
- No interaction between chests

## Intended Behavior

### Core Principle: One Copy, Transceived
- Each item exists as ONE copy in the world
- Items are not duplicated, only moved
- The pool is a shared inventory, partially accessible through chests at any time
- When NPCs prepare chests, they pull from this shared pool

### Item Lifecycle
```
TRASH (gone forever)     RECYCLE (back to pool)
        ^                        ^
        |                        |
   destroyed              sold to vendor
   by player              OR chest despawns (no player nearby)
                          OR corpse despawns (no player nearby)
```

NPCs find items left behind when heroes move on. Guards watch the stashes.

### Mancala Distribution
When items enter the pool, distribute to chests round-robin:
1. First item → next available chest
2. Second item → second chest
3. Loop the board? Add another to first chest
4. No chests available? Distribute to existing chests again (more riches in rich piles)

Overflow is NOT saved - it cycles back through the list. Items keep moving
through active chests like a travelling salesman wandering the circuit again.
Each pass adds more to the piles. Eventually players find the riches.

### Vulnerability While Looting
- Opening a chest requires focus (interacting state)
- While interacting: defenseless
- Monsters nearby attack and interrupt
- Successful hit applies DAZE effect
- Dazed players cannot open chests
- Creates tension: someone must guard while others loot
- Trading allowed during chest interaction (cooperation)

### Multi-Player Chest Access
- 2+ players can interact with same chest
- Trading enabled during interaction
- One holds it open, others take what they need
- If holder is dazed, chest snaps shut

